{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>If a fire breaks out.</b> On its own. <b>The one who kindled the blaze shall make full restitution.</b> For the one who kindled the fire was the cause, for had he not kindled the fire, the fire would not have gone out on its own and burned the stack or the standing grain. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted this verse in Bava Kamma concerning the destruction of the Holy Temple, where it is written (Isaiah 64:9): ״בית קדשנו ותפארתנו אשר הללוך אבותינו היה לשרפת אש״ — 'our holy house and our glory, wherein our fathers praised You, was given to the burning of fire' — and we caused it, for we corrupted; and the Holy One, blessed be He, promised that He will make full restitution, as though He Himself had kindled the blaze."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:02:50.926661304Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}